  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1201 PM CST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\nAs of noon CST, temperatures across the area are in the mid to\nupper 30s. There was, once again, some fog scattered across the\narea this morning, but it has since burned off. Winds today are\nexpected to pick up across west river counties and gust between\n30-35 mph out of the southeast. \n\nStill not much going on in the 7 day forecast. Temperatures today \nand Saturday will be right around average with highs in the upper \n30s to upper 40s. Temperatures will start to warm up towards the 50s \nand low 60s Sunday, and continue with above average highs through at \nleast Wednesday. Winds will increase Saturday and spread east to \ncover the rest of central SD with gusts of 30-40. The chance of \ngusts higher than 35 mph is 70-90%, mainly concentrated west river. \nLow pressure moves into the Dakotas Tuesday bringing another \nincrease to winds up to 30-40 mph and reaching from south central SD \nnortheast to the Sisseton Hills/Prairie Coteau region. This low will \nalso bring some widespread chances for rain Wednesday \nafternoon/evening into Thursday morning with some snow mixing in \npotentially across north central SD. This is still 5/6 days out, so \nkeep an eye on the forecast.",
